#import "../data.typ": *

Tor and VPNs hide where a user connects from, not what the user says. Using only free-tier models and no technical effort, an adversary in our study inferred personal attributes from comments with a mean best-model accuracy of #pct(mean_best("best_original")), covering attributes that an IP address never reveals. A single rewrite before posting reduced this to #pct(mean_best("best_rewritten")) but left every attribute partly exposed. Anonymity tools that care about their users' privacy should treat text as part of the attack surface, for example by offering a local "rewrite before posting" step and warning users that their words, not only their address, identify them. Code, prompts and all raw model outputs are available for anyone to rerun or extend.
